["er.record/1",{"commit":{"envelope":{"actor":"agent:claude-decomposer-p4-operator-surface","causation":"cmd-child-649dc097078e139fd65a9d010646109a5bdf30b49dc1ad68257fedcc8aa19327","correlation":"protocol-artifact-body","record":{"changed":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"intent":{"causation":null,"command_id":"cmd-child-649dc097078e139fd65a9d010646109a5bdf30b49dc1ad68257fedcc8aa19327","command_type":"aep.entity.update/v1","correlation_id":"protocol-artifact-body","execution_id":null,"expected_revision":null,"payload":{"changes":{"body":"## Question\n\nIn a graph projection, is a relation assertion (`Subject::Node` + `Predicate::Relation(edge type)` + `Object::Node`) the same edge as an `ekr.graph.Edge` whose `source`, `type_id` and `target` match it, or are the two always separate things?\n\n## Why nobody can read the answer\n\n- `systems/ekr/domains/graph.yaml` declares `ekr.graph.Edge` with relations `type`, `from` and `to`, and `ekr.graph.Assertion` with `subject_kind`/`subject`, `predicate_kind`/`predicate` and `object_kind`/`object_ref` as plain fields. No `relations:` entry links a relation assertion to an Edge.\n- In code, the type validator checks a relation assertion only against the edge type declaration (source and target types), never against an existing Edge: `crates/ekr-kernel/src/validate/types.rs:234`. Nothing in `crates/ekr-graph/src/assertion.rs` or `edge.rs` joins the two.\n- So an Edge may exist with no relation assertion, a relation assertion may exist with no Edge, and several of either may share one (source, edge type, target). The cardinality of the correspondence, and whether it exists at all, is undecided.\n\nThe operator's prototype viewer merges them (its edges carry `lifecycle`, `valid_from`, `valid_to`, `evidence` and a `has_edge` flag), which is one implementation's answer, not a decision.\n\n## Options\n\n1. **Separate.** Edges are Edges; relation assertions are assertions on their subject node that name an object node. A projection never merges them.\n2. **Join by key.** A projection edge is keyed by (source, edge type, target) and carries every Edge and every relation assertion with that key; `has_edge` says whether an Edge exists. The one-to-many sides must then be stated (several Edges per key, several assertions per key).\n3. **Model change.** A relation assertion names its Edge (for example `Subject::Edge`, or an edge id on the assertion), decided in `ekr.graph` and not in a projection.\n\n## What it stops\n\nAny projection or viewer behaviour that merges a relation assertion into an Edge, or treats one as the other, and the edge-level `lifecycle`, `valid_from`, `valid_to`, `evidence` and `has_edge` fields the prototype carries. No story is drafted for that part.\n\nThe first P4 slice (`story:graph-projection-specification`, `story:graph-projection-renderer`, `story:ekr-view-server`, `story:data-free-graph-viewer`) does not depend on the answer: it projects each Edge and each Assertion exactly as the store holds them and joins neither to the other. Whichever option is chosen, the join arrives as a later story and, if it changes the document, a new version of `ekr.graph-projection`.\n"},"command":"update-entity","target":"ent-42e2af7b6ad949dcd06ce9398d722e0d"},"target":null,"task":null},"result":{"affected":["ent-42e2af7b6ad949dcd06ce9398d722e0d@3"],"audit":["aud-a7606277da79e369078e840f243d0ed6"],"command_id":"cmd-child-649dc097078e139fd65a9d010646109a5bdf30b49dc1ad68257fedcc8aa19327","consistency":"seq-000000000000","events":["evt-a7605f77da79de50078e830f243d0d23"],"outcome":"accepted"}},"lifecycle_state":"recorded"}},"command":{"command":"create","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"intent":{"causation":null,"command_id":"cmd-child-649dc097078e139fd65a9d010646109a5bdf30b49dc1ad68257fedcc8aa19327","command_type":"aep.entity.update/v1","correlation_id":"protocol-artifact-body","execution_id":null,"expected_revision":null,"payload":{"changes":{"body":"## Question\n\nIn a graph p